{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there","id":1431670,"title":"So, how many fera out there?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-10T03:52:39-08:00","id":1431670,"title":"So, how many fera out there?","content":"We roughly know how many werewolves there are out there. Storyteller's handbook gives us an average 15k werewolves alive, which can be scaled up to 20k or down to 10k, depending on wheter the storyteller wants a more or less desperate setting.<br /> Tribes size goes from 500 (Stargazers) to 2000 (Bone Gnawers).<br /> <br /> And that is fine. But do we have any canonical statement for the others Fera? I know that as a rule of thumb the Ratkin should be the most numerous among them, while some breed like the Ajaba should be almost extinct.<br /> <br /> Ah, I'm searching for canonic answers, so nothing like &quot;as many as you need&quot;. I just want to know if the setting has ever spilled some hard numbers about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-10-2021, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T10:00:14-08:00","id":1431699,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think there is an official count in canon. Unlike the Garou, the Fera are not one Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T10:40:00-08:00","id":1431706,"title":"","content":"The number gauges regarding which &quot;X&quot; supernatural in White Wolf books have always been a not really necessary or useful part of the franchise as a whole. For the Fera (which I admittedly find more interesting in some cases, but not all) don't even have canonical sources so what you're asking for is frankly moot. So essentially despite not asking for it, you DO have to go by &quot;as many as you need&quot; for this situation. One tip I'll say is affirming what you said; Ratkin definitely (and realistically) would be the most numerous shape-changers in the oWoD universe. Corax would be the second most. For the rest of the Fera... you'll more or less have to judgment call for yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 01-10-2021, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:47:03-08:00","id":1431723,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Corax have that thing with the eggs. They need a whole Rite in order to breed a new Corax. So they might not be that common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T12:36:11-08:00","id":1431739,"title":"","content":"Ajaba were almost wiped out.. they are also the most fertile of Fera. Canonically if 2 Kinfolk breed they have a 1/3 chance of an Ajaba even if a single kinfolk has a relatively high chance. Kinfolk and Ajaba is higher(though not explicitly given) now bare in mind Ajaba are not like Garou... their majority was beast breed so one might see a pack spawn on average one Ajaba a year.. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T00:53:39-08:00","id":1431803,"title":"","content":"As others mentioned, I don't think numbers are ever mentioned. But there are commentary about their numbers you can use as a guide.<br /> <br /> The other Changing Breeds are always mentioned to be &quot;few&quot;. I always took that to mean that the Garou were at least equal to the population of all other Changing Breeds combined and possibly superior to all of them. But I admit that is only an interpretation. In my head, that comes to between one-third and one-half of the total population of all Changers. But that's just my own made up number.<br /> <br /> The Bastet seem to be the only Breed that was able to hold their own to the Garou, so I interpret that to mean they are of sufficient number to hold territory. So collectively they should be the most numerous, though not enough to equal the Garou. Their numbers seem less because they're present in areas where there's not wolves. There's not many areas where they interact, though they still exist (cougars in the American West, tigers in Asia, jaguars in Mexico, etc.).<br /> <br /> The Nuwisha are like a 14th tribe of Garou, so I would put their numbers as if they were one of the smaller tribes.<br /> <br /> We know that many think the Ananasi and Nagah are destroyed, so they likely have the fewest numbers. First edition PG calls the Ananasi &quot;extremely rare.&quot;<br /> <br /> The depiction of the Gurahl have been all over the place. Earlier material presented them as being almost destroyed, but later editions walked that back. Still, they are likely one of the smaller Breeds.<br /> <br /> Corax were only supposed to be in noticeable numbers on the British Isles and the Pacific Northwest of North America. So if you figure out how many Garou are in those locations, the Corax should only be a fraction of that number. Then increase it a little bit to account for a remnant population elsewhere.<br /> <br /> These are the guidelines I use.<br /> <br /> One issue with a population of the Changing Breeds is that as the game developed, things changed. From the first edition Player's Guide that introduced most of them, there is an emphasis on their low numbers. But as they were developed in the Breedbooks, I don't think that was kept in real consideration. The writers were more interested in developing them just as much as the Garou were, so the presentation implies their numbers are larger than they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  Edited an error I made 01-11-2021, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T07:42:20-08:00","id":1431829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1431803#post1431803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nuwisha are like a 14th tribe of Garou, so I would put their numbers as if they were one of the smaller tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there not a limit on the number of Nuwisha on earth, that is not exceeded? The other remain somewhere within the Umbra. I vaguely remember something like this at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T11:10:50-08:00","id":1431850,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s 100 Nuwisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T11:59:34-08:00","id":1431854,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I assume that is in the Breedbook as it's not in the Players Guides (that I can see). The PGs do state much of the tribe is in the umbra though - exploring the Deep Umbra like the Wagnerians do. But there's all sorts of strange umbra rules about staying too long now that I don't think existed when this concept was first introduced. So and ST needs to play around with that to get things to work, but it's not that difficult to do so. But I assume we can still keep higher numbers for Nuwisha as long as we place them in the umbra and not on the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T13:37:47-08:00","id":1431870,"title":"","content":"I think I saw it in W20 Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T20:37:24-08:00","id":1431910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1431803#post1431803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One issue with a population of the Changing Breeds is that as the game developed, things changed. From the first edition Player's Guide that introduced most of them, there is an emphasis on their low numbers. But as they were developed in the Breedbooks, I don't think that was kept in real consideration. The writers were more interested in developing them just as much as the Garou were, so the presentation implies their numbers are larger than they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The other issue is WWs general inconistancy between IC and OOC information. Fera are few and far between.. for garou. Most have little reason to interact but the very idea that wererats are rarer than wolves is the sort of thing that I can't imagine. Even if you wiped out Rats to the point there was ONE left.. they breed... fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T00:03:14-08:00","id":1431934,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t the same apply for the Ananasi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T02:35:35-08:00","id":1431941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1431850#post1431850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019s 100 Nuwisha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right. I don\u2019t recall the exact number off the top of my head, but Coyote put a hard limit on how many can be in the physical at any one time. And the fallen Nuwisha can force one of the unfallen to have to retreat to the Umbra simply by deciding to move to the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T19:17:19-08:00","id":1432158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1431934#post1431934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t the same apply for the Ananasi?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed.... just because the spiders aren't engaging with the Garou doesn't mean they are.... rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:29:53-07:00","id":1478418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1431941#post1431941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds about right. I don\u2019t recall the exact number off the top of my head, but Coyote put a hard limit on how many can be in the physical at any one time. And the fallen Nuwisha can force one of the unfallen to have to retreat to the Umbra simply by deciding to move to the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told, having them be somewhere between Silent Striders and Stargazers in numbers wouldn't change things immensely even without the &quot;cap on tribemates on prime material plane&quot;, i guess.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In fact, &quot;somewhere between Silent Striders and Stargazers in numbers&quot; works fine as benchmark for most Fera breed populations in one's games, in absence of any fluff motivating the ST to tweak things higher or lower in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-26-2022, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T21:16:30-07:00","id":1479528,"title":"","content":"Going on a random aside while we discuss Fera and Garou tribes, do the Bone Gnawers really make a good case for their individual identity and weight as a tribe of their own or could they work just as well as a Glass Walker camp?<br /> <br /> It's a little something that has been (pardon the pun) gnawing at my thoughts of late and would really like to hear the thoughts and opinions of other people, who might more familiar or up to date, on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-26-2022, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T22:44:45-07:00","id":1479532,"title":"","content":"IMO there's more differences between BG and GW than, say, GF and Fia, Or SL and SF, or Wen and GF. Or CoG and... so on and so forth. They're both city wolf-tribes, but the difference is much more extreme than almost any of the wolves that live out of the city, with notable exceptions in the RT and SG.<br /> <br /> A big part of BG identiy is that most are basically ronin who've nominally pledged themselves to Rat in order to escape the label. A big part of GW identity is that they think their way is right enough that they can push through with weaver ideology despite heavy resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T23:09:14-07:00","id":1479533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1479528#post1479528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going on a random aside while we discuss Fera and Garou tribes, do the Bone Gnawers really make a good case for their individual identity and weight as a tribe of their own or could they work just as well as a Glass Walker camp?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed the Bone Gnawers theme as the &quot;omega tribe&quot; or &quot;runts of the litter&quot; rather than &quot;urban tribe&quot; so I don't view them as the same as the Glass Walkers. Those are two different themes. <br /> <br /> In addition, I often interpret the Glass Walkers as less than an urban tribe as &quot;wolves in sheep clothing&quot; meaning werewolves that hide their identity very well to live among mankind (since Cockroach is very big on living unseen among humanity). So while both today are seen as &quot;urban tribes&quot;, they have very different aspects. The &quot;urban tribes&quot; theme are an emergent property, not an essential one and these two tribes slot into that in very different ways.<br /> <br /> That's not how it's been developed in the tribebooks, but I like my interpretation better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T23:19:06-07:00","id":1479534,"title":"","content":"I agree. BG and GW have totally different mentalities, for the most part. The GW derived from the &quot;Warder of Man&quot;-Packs that septs historically send to the human settlements to guard them and that became fascinated with progress and spirits that arose from this. Their tribal identity was dominated by the Wise Guys for a while, but now this mentality is resurfacing.<br /> <br /> The BG, on the other hand, derive from all the omegas, who were driven out of their septs for not making the cut. Either formally expelled or just runaways or garou who couldn't handle the sept's expectations. They formed their own culture, revolving around them being the sturdiest of the garou for all the hardship they endured and the camaraderie they experience.<br /> <br /> So, in a nutshell, the GW are city-dwellers because they want to explore this terrain, while BG didn't have a choice as to life there, where other garou tribes didn't claim territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T07:00:44-07:00","id":1479542,"title":"","content":"Would I to make changes to the BG, I would make them into either a cross tribal Camp within all the tribes, or basically use them as a kind of Ronin Camp for lore purposes. That would make far more sense than linking them to the GW specifically. I have far more trouble picturing them as fully recognized as Nation members (and a tribe on top of that) than picturing them as distinct from the Glass Walkers (they definitely are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T21:38:49-07:00","id":1479643,"title":"","content":"Fewer than could realistically support their complex society with all their factions. More than could believably keep themselves secret from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T23:26:47-07:00","id":1479647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1479534#post1479534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in a nutshell, the GW are city-dwellers because they want to explore this terrain, while BG didn't have a choice as to life there, where other garou tribes didn't claim territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an excellent summary. Very succinct. I'll try to remember this phrasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1479542#post1479542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">use them as a kind of Ronin Camp for lore purposes</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not too far from the mark for the &quot;Rabble&quot; of the Bone Gnawers, who seem to be essentially Ronin except that the Bone Gnawers decided to perform the Rite of Passage of them just because they think everyone should be able to belong to a tribe. In my view, there is a real tension within the tribe between members who just do not care at all and those who truly want to fulfill some kind of purpose for Gaia.<br /> <br /> I tend to have a much more negative perspective on the Bone Gnawer tribe than those who are content with depicting them as hobo heroes, but it is precisely that negative tension that makes the tribe very interesting in my opinion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T00:07:43-07:00","id":1479648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there?p=1479643#post1479643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fewer than could realistically support their complex society with all their factions. More than could believably keep themselves secret from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Principality of Sealand was big enough to have a government in exile I think a few thousand werewolves can form some cliques and call them factions. And Sealand started small instead of being a remnant of a larger society that formed a lot of its rituals when it was much bigger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T03:08:35-07:00","id":1479877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1431670-so-how-many-fera-out-there#post1431670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do we have any canonical statement for the others Fera?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's 100 Nuwisha in Telluria at one time, I don't know how many of them lives in the Umbra. Also the number of Gurahls is about 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-01-2022, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}